I estimate name-mention rates of **Todoist 65%**, **TickTick 55%**, **Microsoft To Do 45%**, **Google Tasks 40%**, and **Any.do 25%** across these 100 questions.

The strongest triggers are constrained platform and integration queries: Microsoft To Do for Outlook and Microsoft, Google Tasks for Google Calendar, and TickTick and Todoist for desktop, Linux, cross-platform, calendar, reminders, and multiple-device needs. Their official feature pages support those associations: [Microsoft To Do’s Outlook integration](https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/outlook/calendar/create-tasks-with-to-do-in-outlook), [Todoist’s integrations](https://www.todoist.com/integrations), [TickTick’s platform availability](https://ticktick.com/download?language=en_us), and [TickTick’s calendar subscriptions](https://help.ticktick.com/articles/7055781614550253568). Generic “best” and everyday queries also tend to prompt comparisons, creating name mentions even when an app is not the top recommendation. I discounted all five for off-topic or unusual intents such as name ideas, JavaScript examples, game-like lists, and pencil-specific use.

