The prompts with specific integrations or devices shift the rates sharply: Google Calendar and Chromebook questions favor Google Tasks, Outlook and Office questions favor Microsoft To Do, and widgets, calendars, reminders, and Linux favor TickTick or Todoist. Shared lists and family use make Any.do more likely, but few prompts target it directly. These product associations are documented by [Google Tasks Help](https://support.google.com/tasks/answer/7675772?hl=en-GB), [Microsoft Support](https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/outlook/calendar/manage-tasks-with-to-do-in-outlook), [Todoist](https://www.todoist.com/integrations), [TickTick](https://help.ticktick.com/articles/7055780404896202752), and [Any.do](https://www.any.do/en/family).

Across generic recommendation prompts, an assistant would often name several established apps, including as alternatives or comparisons. I estimate the per-question name-mention rate at roughly 40% for Todoist, 30% for TickTick, 28% for Google Tasks, 25% for Microsoft To Do, and 15% for Any.do.

